# Class: obo:CHEBI_166899 (globulin type)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_166899 "One of the major classifications of proteins, which may be further divided into the euglobulins and the pseudoglobulins. The former group is insoluble in water but soluble in saline solutions and may be precipitated in water that has been half-saturated with a salt such as ammonium sulfate. The latter group is soluble in water and has properties that resemble those of the true globulins. Globulins are an important source of protein in seed plants and are found in minute amounts in cereals. Globulins found in animal fluids are enzymes, antibodies, and fibrous and contractile proteins usually contained in the blood plasma.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_166899 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166899 "globulin type")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166899 "globulin type"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_166899 obo:CDNO_0000009)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_166964 (albumin type)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_166964 "Family of globular proteins, the most common of which are the serum albumins. All the proteins of the albumin family are water-soluble, moderately soluble in concentrated salt solutions, and experience heat denaturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_166964 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166964 "albumin type")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166964 "albumin type"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_166964 obo:CDNO_0000009)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_166965 (simple oxygenated xanthones)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_166965 "Simple oxygenated xanthones are subdivided according to the degree of oxygenation into non-, mono-, di-, tri-, tetra-, penta-, and hexaoxygenated substances. In these xanthones the substituents are simple hydroxy, methoxy, or methyl groups. About 150 simple oxygenated xanthones have been reported.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_166965 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166965 "simple oxygenated xanthones")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166965 "simple oxygenated xanthones"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_166965 obo:CHEBI_51149)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_166966 (prenylated and related xanthones)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_166966 "These xanthones are usually restricted to the plant species of the family Guttiferae. The major C5 unit of the substituents included the commonly found 3-methylbut-2-enyl or isoprenyl group as in isoemericellin and the less frequent 3-hydroxy-3-methylbutyl as in nigrolineaxanthone P and 1,1-dimethylprop-2-enyl as in globuxanthone, respectively.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_166966 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166966 "prenylated and related xanthones")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166966 "prenylated and related xanthones"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_166966 obo:CHEBI_51149)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_166967 (cis-fatty acid)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_166967 "A cis configuration means that the two hydrogen atoms adjacent to the double bond stick out on the same side of the chain. The rigidity of the double bond freezes its conformation and, in the case of the cis isomer, causes the chain to bend and restricts the conformational freedom of the fatty acid. The more double bonds the chain has in the cis configuration, the less flexibility it has. When a chain has many cis bonds, it becomes quite curved in its most accessible conformations.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_166967 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166967 "cis-fatty acid")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166967 "cis-fatty acid"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_166967 obo:CHEBI_35366)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_166968 (trans-fatty acid)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_166968 "A trans configuration in contrast to the cis, means that the adjacent two hydrogen atoms lie on opposite sides of the chain. As a result, they do not cause the chain to bend much, and their shape is similar to straight saturated fatty acids.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_166968 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166968 "trans-fatty acid")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_166968 "trans-fatty acid"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_166968 obo:CHEBI_35366)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_16709 (pyridoxine)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_16709 "A hydroxymethylpyridine with hydroxymethyl groups at positions 4 and 5, a hydroxy group at position 3 and a methyl group at position 2. The 4-methanol form of vitamin B6, it is converted intoto pyridoxal phosphate which is a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters, sphingolipids and aminolevulinic acid.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_16709 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_16709 "pyridoxine")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_16709 "pyridoxine"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_16709 obo:CHEBI_27306)

