# Class: obo:CHEBI_17015 (riboflavin)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_17015 "D-Ribitol in which the hydroxy group at position 5 is substituted by a 7,8-dimethyl-2,4-dioxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[g]pteridin-10(2H)-yl moiety. It is a nutritional factor found in milk, eggs, malted barley, liver, kidney, heart, and leafy vegetables, but the richest natural source is yeast. The free form occurs only in the retina of the eye, in whey, and in urine; its principal forms in tissues and cells are as flavin mononucleotide and flavin-adenine dinucleotide.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_17015 obo:cdno.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_17015 "riboflavin")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CHEBI_17015 "riboflavin"^^xsd:string)
SubClassOf(obo:CHEBI_17015 obo:CHEBI_176838)

# Class: obo:CHEBI_17020 (glucomannan)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_17020 "A heteroglycan consisting of beta-(1->4)-linked D-glucose (G) and D-mannose (M) in a proportion of 5:8. The basic polymeric repeating unit has the pattern: GGMMGMMMMMGGM, with branching through beta-(1->3)- and beta-(1->6)-glucosyl linkages. Acetate groups are present on C-6 every 9-19 units of the main chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:CHEBI_17020 obo:cdno.owl)
