# Class: obo:CHEBI_73558 (D3 vitamins)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CHEBI_73558 "A vitamin D that is calciol or its hydroxylated metabolites calcidiol and calcitriol. Calciol (also known as vitamin D3) acts as a hormone precursor, being hydroxylated in the liver to calcidiol (25-hydroxyvitamin D3), which is then further hydroxylated in the kidney to give calcitriol (1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3), the active hormone.")
